.TH SCADO 1 "August 23, 2026" "VirtualSquare Labs"
.SH NAME
scado \- manage per-user executable capability authorizations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scado -e
|
.B -l
|
.B -D
.br
.B scado -u
.I /absolute/command
|
.B -U
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B scado
manages the current user's protected authorization file used by
.BR "cado -S" .
Exactly one action is required and trailing operands are rejected.
.PP
Each persisted noncomment entry has exactly two or three colon-delimited fields:
.nf
    absolute path : capability-list
    absolute path : capability-list : 64-hexadecimal-character SHA-256
.fi
.PP
An optional trailing
.B #
starts a comment. Field-edge whitespace is ignored. Internal path spaces are
permitted and backslashes are literal. Paths must be absolute. Capability lists
use the strict grammar described in
.BR cado (1).
A persisted digest is absent or exactly 64 hexadecimal characters; an empty
persisted digest is invalid.
.PP
During
.B scado -e
only, an empty third field requests SHA-256 calculation. The value is filled
before installation and never persists empty. After the editor exits, scado
hashes the edited input, authenticates, then hashes the exact input consumed
while rendering a mode-0600 staging file in the protected spool. It syncs the
file, renames it atomically, and syncs the directory. A changed input, invalid
line, digest failure, or output failure leaves the old scado file untouched.
Every post-editor failure preserves and reports the editable recovery copy.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -e , " --edit"
Edit with
.BR $VISUAL ,
then
.BR $EDITOR ,
then the configured default editor.
.TP
.BR -l , " --list"
Copy the current scado file to standard output without changing standard output
flags.
.TP
.BR -D , " --delete"
Authenticate and delete the current user's scado file.
.TP
.BI "-u " /absolute/command
.TQ
.BI "--update " /absolute/command
Authenticate and recompute the matching persisted digest. A missing path or an
entry without a digest is an error.
.TP
.BR -U , " --update-all"
Authenticate and recompute every persisted digest.
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Print usage and exit.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
    /bin/ping : cap_net_raw
    /usr/local/bin/tool : net_admin : dcb237f1cb20ee7b1550900d1b524c554063fd17fc673c56d341736ced6bed4b
    /opt/my tool : chown : # filled during scado -e
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cado (1),
.BR capabilities (7)
